This product includes software developed by Jason S. Wrench as part of the
OpenStage suite of free tools for higher education.

The engine (@openstage/assess) has no third-party runtime dependencies. It
uses only the Node.js standard library. The app (@openstage/app) has none
either.

The desktop window (packages/app/shell) is a Tauri shell. It is built with
Tauri and the Rust crates Tauri depends on, which are released under the MIT
and Apache 2.0 licences and others of the same kind, and it shows the app in
the Microsoft Edge WebView2 runtime that Windows provides. The installer also
carries a copy of Node.js (MIT licence), the program that runs the app, so that
a computer needs nothing installed. None of this is part of the engine, which
runs without it.

The plain-text import profile reads the standard test-bank text format: the
plain-text question layout that many publisher test banks follow, a de facto
convention rather than a published standard. Apart from the icons below, no
third-party code, text or data is included in this project, and this project is
not affiliated with or endorsed by any other software vendor.

The look of the app (the navy bar, the menus, the command search and the
colours, 2026-11-11) is the OpenStage suite's. The menu bar, the menu button
and the command search (packages/app/ui/menubar.js, popupmenu.js and
commandsearch.js) are copied from OpenStage Author (editor/src/menubar.ts,
popupmenu.ts and commandsearch.ts) by way of OpenExplainer's copies, written
again as plain JavaScript; the suite's colours and sizes
(packages/app/ui/openstage-ui.css) are a copy of Author's
design/openstage-ui.css. Both are by the same author and under the same
Apache 2.0 licence.

